@startuml animate-stick-figure-events
title Stick Figure Dance — Event Flow
autonumber
actor User
participant "Python CLI\nmain()" as CLI
participant "load_jsonl()" as Loader
participant "make_html()" as Builder
database "Local JSONL" as JSONL
file "Generated HTML" as HTML
participant "Browser UI\nCanvas + JavaScript" as Browser

User -> CLI : Run script with input/output paths
CLI -> CLI : Resolve paths and validate
CLI -> JSONL : Check input exists
CLI -> Loader : load_jsonl(input)
Loader -> JSONL : Read each line (UTF-8)
loop Each non-empty line
  Loader -> Loader : Parse JSON object
  Loader -> Loader : Normalize landmarks + timestamp
end
Loader -> Loader : Sort frames by timestamp_ms
Loader --> CLI : frames[]
CLI -> Builder : make_html(frames, title)
Builder -> Builder : Serialize frames and connections
Builder -> Builder : Compose standalone HTML/CSS/JS
Builder --> CLI : HTML string
CLI -> HTML : Create parent directory and write file
CLI --> User : Print frame count, duration, output path
User -> Browser : Open generated HTML locally
Browser -> Browser : draw() first frame
alt Click Play
  loop While playing
    Browser -> Browser : requestAnimationFrame(tick)
    Browser -> Browser : Advance elapsed time by speed
    Browser -> Browser : Find nearest timestamped frame
    Browser -> Browser : draw() bones, joints, status
  end
else Seek / Restart
  User -> Browser : Change slider or click Restart
  Browser -> Browser : Set current frame / elapsed time
  Browser -> Browser : draw()
end
note over JSONL,HTML
Input is read-only. Output is a separate HTML file.
Playback is client-side and makes no network requests.
end note
@enduml
